  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Eight point charges of charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> each are placed on the eight corners of a cube of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>. A solid neutral metallic sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is placed with its centre at the centre of the cube. As a result, charges are induced on the sphere, which form a certain pattern on its surface. The electric&nbsp;potential of the sphere is</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
